    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "story",
        "type": "story",
        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "A toy made of parts"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "A toy rocket is a cone on a cylinder, a medicine capsule is a cylinder with two hemispheres. Joining solids changes which surfaces are visible."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "CSA formulas",
          "basic solids",
          "capsule",
          "cone on cylinder",
          "hemisphere on cube",
          "hidden surface",
          "list visible faces",
          "square units"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "The basic solids are cuboid, cube, cylinder, cone, sphere and hemisphere.\nCurved surface area of a cylinder is 2 pi r h, of a cone is pi r l with l = root(r^2 + h^2), of a sphere is 4 pi r^2 and of a hemisphere is 2 pi r^2.\nWhen two solids are joined, the area where they join is hidden, so it is not part of the total surface area.\nFor a cone on a cylinder: TSA = CSA of cone + CSA of cylinder + area of the base circle of the cylinder.\nFor a capsule: TSA = CSA of cylinder + CSA of two hemispheres.\nFor a hemisphere on a cube, subtract the circle covered on the cube, then add the curved area of the hemisphere.\nDraw the combined solid and list which surfaces are visible before you calculate.\nUse the same units everywhere and write square units."
        }
      },
